Libraries and runtime
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

J2K Desktop uses Kotlin, Compose Multiplatform, kotlinx.coroutines,
kotlinx.serialization, OkHttp, Okio, Jsoup, Coil, RxJava, Injekt,
apk-parser and dex2jar, each under its own license (mostly Apache 2.0).
The release builds bundle a Java runtime (OpenJDK, GPLv2 with the Classpath
Exception); its license files are included with it under lib/runtime/legal.

The name "Tachiyomi" and related names belong to their owners. J2K Desktop
is an independent project and is not affiliated with Tachiyomi, Mihon or
TachiyomiJ2K.
